; WildGrassCactus — 1st of 3 sand/desert-flavor Wild grass variants (content-variety pass
; Task 9, 2026-08-26). See wild_grass.tres's own header for the model_scenes array change.
;
; STRUCTURE: instances the existing res://assets/terrain/wild_grass/WildGrass.tscn verbatim
; as a child (identity transform — same grass-base reuse pattern Task 8's
; WaterLilypad1.tscn/WaterLilypad2.tscn use for Water.tscn: "don't duplicate the base scene,
; instance it"). This scene does NOT touch WildGrass.tscn itself. Plus ONE centered desert
; prop, same "single centered specimen" convention CommonTree1.tscn/Bush.tscn already use
; for their own Model node (scale-only transform, no rotation, no XZ offset).
;
; Source: "Cactus_1.fbx", Ultimate Nature Pack by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — the task
; brief's own research directly confirmed this filename in this pack before the task started
; (unlike Palm/Coconut below, which needed an on-disk audit). License.txt re-checked at
; `source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../License.txt` before import, per
; asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate (CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain Dedication, same
; boilerplate as every other Quaternius pack in this repo). Recorded in
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres (extends that pack's
; existing assets_used list). Flat vertex-color materials ("Green"/"LightOrange" per the
; source .mtl) — no texture files to carry over, same as Bush.fbx/Rock_Moss_N.fbx precedent.
;
; RAW SOURCE LOCATION: copied to res://assets/terrain/wild_grass_cactus/Cactus_1.fbx (a
; single-use prop, not shared across multiple composed scenes, so it lives directly
; alongside this scene rather than in a shared per-model folder — same convention
; CropCactus2.tscn/Cactus_2.fbx already established for single-use crop props).
;
; SCALE: raw Cactus_1.fbx measured local-space AABB (one-off SceneTree script,
; res://tests/_measure_wild_grass_props.gd, deleted after use, same corner-transform
; procedure Task 8's clearance fix used) = size (0.549685, 1.00763, 0.562914), position
; (-0.267189, -0.010727, -0.281552) — a single specimen ~1.0 raw units tall. Scaled to a
; ~0.5-tile target height (scale 0.496213): shorter than every Forest tree's ~2.2-2.5-tile
; canopy convention (this is a squat desert succulent, not a canopy tree) but taller than
; the wild-grass clusters it stands among (WildGrass.tscn's own ~0.065 blade-height
; baseline), matching Bush.tscn's "distinct scale-class from ground cover" reasoning at a
; shorter absolute height since a cactus reads smaller than a bush. Resulting footprint
; ~0.273 x 0.279 tile-units — a compact single-specimen silhouette, not tile-covering.
; Y-offset (0.005324 = scale * |raw AABB base y|) nudges the model up so its measured base
; sits exactly on the slab's y=0 top surface rather than sinking fractionally into it (raw
; pivot is very close to, but not exactly at, the mesh base). FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a
; measured GDD number — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: whether a single cactus reads as "something
; to claim, without reading as broken" on wild grass specifically, per Open Question #29's
; exact wording (WildGrass.tscn's own header) — the same open question every prior
; scale/placement judgment call in this pass carries, sharper here since this is the first
; time a desert-flavor prop sits on a grass-family (not sand) terrain base.
;
; NO SLAB WRAPPER NEEDED HERE: unlike a land terrain built from scratch, WildGrass.tscn's
; own ground/patch geometry already lives under a node named "Slab" inside the instanced
; scene itself (see that scene's own header — the OcclusionFader exemption mechanism is
; internal to WildGrass.tscn, not something this wrapper scene needs to reproduce). The
; cactus prop sits as a plain sibling of the WildGrass instance, same "no Slab wrapper
; needed" reasoning WaterLilypad1.tscn's header already established for its lilypad props.
